SQLite/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files that ARE tracked on purpose even though a broader rule above would
# otherwise hide them (found while building tests/test-no-tracked-scratch.js)
#
# ELI5: a few small placeholder files live inside folders we tell git to
# mostly ignore. The empty `.gitkeep` files just hold a folder's shape in
# git (git does not track empty folders at all); the `.htaccess` files stop
# a web server from listing or serving that folder's contents. Both were
# committed once, on purpose, before the broader rule existed — and, same
# as the story at the top of this file, adding a rule afterwards does not
# untrack a file git is already following. The difference here is that
# that is exactly what was wanted, so it is written down below instead of
# being an accident nobody explained.
#
# Detail: `appWeb/data_share/*` (added for the DB-direct rewrite so the
# regenerated song/setlist data isn't committed) and `SQLite/` (added so the
# legacy password-hash copy is never committed) both also match these
# scaffolding files as an unintended side effect of being broad, directory-
# wide patterns. A negation on the FILE alone is not enough here — git's own
# rule is "it is not possible to re-include a file if a parent directory of
# that file is excluded" (see `git help gitignore`), and `SQLite/` and the
# `*` in `appWeb/data_share/*` both exclude the FOLDER as a whole, not just
# its contents. So each folder is re-opened (`!folder/`) and then
# immediately re-closed one level down (`folder/*`) before naming the one
# or two files that should stay tracked — NEVER just `!folder/` on its own,
# because on `SQLite/` in particular that would blank-check the very folder
# `data_health_admin.php` writes the real password-hash-bearing
# `ihymns.db` into, undoing the whole reason that rule exists. With the
# `folder/*` re-close in place, only the named files are exempt — anything
# else dropped into these folders (a stray export, a real ihymns.db) is
# still ignored exactly as before.
!appWeb/data_share/.htaccess
!appWeb/data_share/SQLite/
appWeb/data_share/SQLite/*
!appWeb/data_share/SQLite/.gitkeep
!appWeb/data_share/SQLite/.htaccess
!appWeb/data_share/setlist_json/
appWeb/data_share/setlist_json/*
!appWeb/data_share/setlist_json/.gitkeep
!appWeb/data_share/setlist_json/.htaccess
!appWeb/data_share/song_data/
appWeb/data_share/song_data/*
!appWeb/data_share/song_data/.gitkeep
!appWeb/data_share/song_data/.htaccess

# The vendored mPDF engine (rule #39 — vendored under appWeb/private_html/lib/
# outside every web docroot, committed wholesale because shared hosting has
# no Composer step at deploy time) ships its OWN `tmp/` folder (mPDF's
# working-file cache, upstream's placeholder to keep it present) and its
# `paragonie/random_compat` dependency ships its OWN `dist/` folder (signing
# keys for that package's release, nothing to do with OUR build output).
# Those folder names collide with this project's generic "ignore build/cache
# output named tmp/ or dist/" rules above, purely by coincidence of naming.
# Same open-then-reclose shape as above: mPDF actually WRITES working files
# into its `tmp/` folder at runtime, so a bare `!tmp/` would start tracking
# whatever it drops there next time someone runs `git add`. Re-closing with
# `tmp/*` keeps that safe and exempts only the one placeholder file it ships.
!appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/mpdf/mpdf/tmp/
appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/mpdf/mpdf/tmp/*
!appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/mpdf/mpdf/tmp/.gitignore
!appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/paragonie/random_compat/dist/
appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/paragonie/random_compat/dist/*
!appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/paragonie/random_compat/dist/random_compat.phar.pubkey
!appWeb/private_html/lib/pdf/vendor/paragonie/random_compat/dist/random_compat.phar.pubkey.asc

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendor libraries — generated by tools/download-vendor.sh (#354 / #526)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bootstrap, FontAwesome, jQuery, Animate.css, Fuse.js, Tone.js, PDF.js
# downloaded as PWA offline-fallback for the onerror handlers in index.php.
# Re-generated on every deploy by deploy.yml; do not commit.
appWeb/public_html/vendor/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python bytecode (#967)
# Generated by `python3 -m py_compile` or normal module imports. One .pyc
# was accidentally committed under .importers/scrapers/__pycache__/ in
# the past; this rule prevents recurrence and untracks the orphan via
# the accompanying `git rm`.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub Wiki sibling clone (#958)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub stores wikis as a separate git repo (`<project>.wiki.git`); cloning
# it alongside the main repo lets Claude / IDEs read wiki content without a
# network round-trip. The clone is its own repository — never commit it
# inside the main repo.
# Directory form (no trailing /*) is required to suppress an *embedded git
# repo* — a nested clone is a gitlink that `iHymns.wiki/*` does not ignore.
iHymns.wiki/
iHymns.wiki/*
iHymns.wiki.git/
iHymns.wiki.git/*